{"seq":11,"trial_id":"anatomy-instruction-route-2026-11/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-route-hook-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r5","wall_ts":"2026-10-30T20:41:29.258Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"ad23c853f0ac67673addd82bbef08175bbbf8246c28007799f9f6fe1a5d0b15c","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DANATOM0001","text":"Here are the Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers I found in Moss's notes. I searched the notes in GBrain (keyword search, so a phrasing I didn't try could still be missing):\n\n1. **#4419**, gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. Source: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated),\" which says it was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. The \"Q2 expansion wrap (belated)\" note from Marcus Lindqvist (14 Jul 2025) also lists #4419 but describes it as \"Gate 3 printer lag,\" so the two notes disagree on what the ticket is. Worth confirming with Thea before it goes in the weekly notes.\n2. **#PD-4492**, Pemberline Dock gatehouse kiosk alerts at the Eau Claire yard, where drivers at Doors 14–18 weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Thea Ramaswell submitted it on 4 Oct 2025, support patched it, and she confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift cleared. Source: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). That note also has a follow-up to review the Eau Claire kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n\nI left out ticket #4409 and #4412. They appear in Moss's Central handoff notes and belong to a different account. I also left out \"Quarendon Freightways,\" which is a different company and not a Pemberline customer.\n\nMoss's notes are addressed to Ruth Calloway, so I've only passed along the ticket numbers and what they're about, not the notes themselves."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DANATOM0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
